  "notes": "Two parallel weld failures (FW-10 undersized/fatigue, FW-60 fatigue) both feed the same downstream instrument-air-loss failure mode, per rule 5's parallel-trigger pattern (though here two origins converge rather than one trigger diverging). Block-13 lists two rows: cause B (manufacturer B130/Bechtel, FW-10) and cause X (manufacturer F155/Senior Flexonics, FW-60); official cause_code/category per FORM-366 top-level fields is B/Design-Manufacturing-Installation, applied to the cause node per rule 4, though FW-60 weld failure (cause X per block 13) is still linked via CAUSED_BY to the same single Cause node since only one Cause node is created from the authoritative top-level cause_code/category. No BACKED_UP_BY edge modeled: the redundant RPS subsystem remaining capable is safety-analysis context about which channel remained operable, not a distinct backup System per se -- captured in chain summary only. Previous-occurrence LER keys use the docket-unit form as literally stated (e.g., '50-388/2015-004-00' -> key '1-2015-004-00') per instructions to preserve leading unit digit."
